            <ArticleTitle>Gated magnetic resonance imaging for assessment of cardiac function and myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>449-57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gated magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) is a promising noninvasive imaging modality capable of evaluating cardiac function and blood flow in the great vessels. MRI detects acute and chronic myocardial infarctions in experimental animals and in man.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
